===============================================================================
Modifications in this fork (Zero Zone deployment)
===============================================================================

This fork adds, among other things, an OPTIONAL live-stream feature to the Export
API (sqreader/livehub.py, sqreader/live_fake.py, scripts/live_bench.py and the
live/* parts of sqreader/export_api.py, sqreader/httpsrv.py, sqreader/cli.py,
sqreader/config.py). It is a modification of sqreader and is distributed under the
same terms as the rest of this repository: AGPL-3.0-or-later with the Commons
Clause (see LICENSE). It is OFF by default (config export_live_enabled) and, when
on, is served only on the token-protected Export API path, never on a public route.

AGPL note: the live stream is a network interface. If you run a modified version
of this program and let others interact with it remotely through a network, the
AGPL requires you to offer those users the Corresponding Source of the version you
actually run, including these modifications. Keep the exact deployed commit
available (see deploy/zerozone/KURULUM-TR.md, "Lisans notu"). This note is not
legal advice.

The live stream carries raw player data (EOS ids, in-game names, memory
addresses); see PRIVACY.md. The third-party assets listed above are not covered by
this licence and are not part of the live stream.
